: %s (16 default mechanisms; edit scores, targets, evidence and prose)\\n\",\n112:\t\t\"Capability assessment criado: %s (16 mecanismos default; edite scores, targets, evidência e prosa)\\n\"), path)\n116:// assessBaselineCommit resolves HEAD for the scaffold; \"0000000\" when git is\n118:func assessBaselineCommit(root string) string {\n130:type assessReport struct {\n135:\tAssessedAt  string   `json:\"assessed_at\"`\n143:// stable-id contract, staleness. It never writes.\n144:func runAssessValidationIn(files pose.Files, root string) (*assessReport, error) {\n146:\tassessment, err := store.LoadCapabilityAssessment()\n150:\treport := &assessReport{Path: assessment.Path, Mechanisms: len(assessment.Mechanisms), AssessedAt: assessment.AssessedAt}\n151:\treport.Errors = append(report.Errors, store.ValidateCapabilityEvidence(assessment)...)\n159:\t\tfor _, id := range pose.RenumberedMechanisms(latest, assessment) {\n161:\t\t\t\tfmt.Sprintf(\"mechanism %q was published in the latest snapshot but is gone from the assessment; retire it (`- retired: true`) instead of removing it\", id))\n166:\tif assessed, err := time.Parse(\"2006-01-02\", assessment.AssessedAt); err == nil {\n167:\t\treport.AgeDays = int(files.Now().Sub(assessed).Hours() / 24)\n171:\t\t\t\tfmt.Sprintf(\"assessment is %d days old (policy: %d); consider reassessing\", report.AgeDays, policy.StaleAfterDays))\n175:\tif out, err := pose.RawHistoryGit(root, \"rev-list\", \"--count\", assessment.BaselineCommit+\"..HEAD\").Output(); err == nil {\n181:\t\t\t\tfmt.Sprintf(\"baseline_commit is %d commits behind HEAD (policy: %d); consider reassessing\", n, policy.StaleAfterCommits))\n187:// runAssessValidation reads and writes the filesystem directly; runAssessValidationIn takes the\n  1618\t\n  1619\tfunc validationSummaryOf(run validationRunResult) *validationSummary {\n  1620\t\tsummary := &validationSummary{Outcome: run.Outcome}\n  1621\t\tfor _, check := range run.Checks {\n  1622\t\t\tcommand := strings.TrimSpace(check.Program + \" \" + strings.Join(check.Args, \" \"))\n  1623\t\t\tif check.Outcome != \"skipped\" && command != \"\" {\n  1624\t\t\t\tsummary.Commands = append(summary.Commands, command)\n  1625\t\t\t}\n  1626\t\t\tline := \"- [\" + check.Outcome + \"] \" + check.ID\n  1627\t\t\tswitch {\n  1628\t\t\tcase check.SkipReason != \"\":\n  1629\t\t\t\tline += \" (\" + check.SkipReason + \")\"\n  1630\t\t\tcase check.DurationSeconds > 0:\n  1631\t\t\t\tline += fmt.Sprintf(\" (%.1fs)\", check.DurationSeconds)\n  1632\t\t\t}\n  1633\t\t\tif check.ExitCode != nil {\n  1634\t\t\t\tline += fmt.Sprintf(\" exit=%d\", *check.ExitCode)\n  1635\t\t\t}\n  1636\t\t\tsummary.Results = append(summary.Results, line)\n  1637\t\t}\n  1638\t\t// The report records the run's verdict too, built from the outcome rather\n  1639\t\t// than copied from the printed line, so the recorded evidence keeps its\n  1640\t\t// shape while the terminal is free to change.\n  1641\t\tif run.Counts.OptionalFailed > 0 {\n  1642\t\t\tsummary.Results = append(summary.Results, fmt.Sprintf(\"Warning: %d optional check(s) failed.\", run.Counts.OptionalFailed))\n  1643\t\t}\n  1644\t\tswitch run.Outcome {\n  1645\t\tcase \"fail\":\n  1646\t\t\tsummary.Results = append(summary.Results, \"Result: FAILURE (required check failed)\")\n  1647\t\tdefault:\n   250\t\n   251\t### Files and modules changed\n   252\t`pose-mcp/internal/cli` (validate, its scope selection, its result fields and the help catalogue), `pose-mcp/internal/pose` (the delivery reading of the result), the manual in English and pt-BR with their embedded copies, this spec and its ADR.\n   253\t\n   254\t### Validation executed\n   255\tSee the execution log: the package tests with mutation checks, the full `go test ./...` and the strict matrix with 236 of 236 checks.\n   256\t\n   257\t### Residual risks\n   258\tAn instance that declares a module self-contained while its checks read files outside it would carry a stale result. The declaration is explicit and documented, and the default stays the full fallback.\n   259\t\n   260\t### Follow-ups\n   261\t- [open] F1: cover with an end-to-end test that a review bundle sealed over a carried record judges the carried head (seal, verify and closeout-check on a fixture). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n   262\t- [open] F2: `--carry --report` lists carried checks as executed commands without their `carried_from` head and time; exclude them from the executed summary and label reused results (review round 13, N39). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
